{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/s28CustomDebugStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/Se","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/SE","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/SQ","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/SH","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs"]]},"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Structures","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/CycleDecomposition"],"title":"Structures"},{"anchor":"Initializers","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/init(_:)","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/init(successors:)","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/init(vertexCount:successor:)"],"title":"Initializers"},{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/cycleDecomposition()","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/successor(of:)","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/successor(of:steps:)"],"title":"Instance Methods"},{"anchor":"Default-Implementations","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/CustomDebugStringConvertible-Implementations","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/CustomStringConvertible-Implementations","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/Decodable-Implementations","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/DirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/Encodable-Implementations","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/Equatable-Implementations","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/Hashable-Implementations"],"title":"Default Implementations"}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"FunctionalGraph"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Following any vertex’s edges eventually repeats, so each weakly connected component holds"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exactly one cycle, with rooted trees hanging off its vertices (Flajolet and Odlyzko, “Random"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"mapping statistics”, EUROCRYPT ’89). "},{"code":"cycleDecomposition()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" finds every cycle and tree in O(n);"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"successor(of:steps:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" answers f^k(v) for any k."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For f given as a closure over a state space too large to store, use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"floydCycleDetection"},{"type":"text","text":" or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"brentCycleDetection"},{"type":"text","text":", which need only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" states and O(1) memory."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Storage.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" One ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" per vertex, ","type":"text"},{"code":"f(v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The edge leaving ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" has position ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so edge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"positions and edge indices are both the source. For ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" vertex labels, use","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"LabeledGraph<Label, FunctionalGraph>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; ","type":"text"},{"code":"LabeledGraph(FunctionalGraph(g)!, labels: g.vertices)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"gives a graph ","type":"text"},{"code":"g","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" its labels back.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The graph is immutable: build a new one to change f.","type":"text"}]}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The graph of a function f on the vertices "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<n"},{"type":"text","text":": every vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":" has exactly one out-edge,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v → f(v)"},{"type":"text","text":", and a fixed point is a self-loop. Also called a successor graph (Laaksonen,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":", §16.3)."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/functionalgraphs\/functionalgraph"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"FunctionalGraph"}]